The process of converting a non-dairy product into one that is suitable for those with lactose intolerance or who follow a vegan diet can be quite simple, provided the right ingredients and techniques are employed. When converting a recipe to be lactose-free and vegan, there are several things to consider.

Firstly, it's essential to understand what makes a particular product dairy-based. Many dairy products contain casein, a protein derived from cow's milk that is commonly used in food manufacturing due to its unique properties. To replace this ingredient, plant-based proteins such as soy, pea, or rice protein can be utilized. These alternatives provide similar functionalities while remaining suitable for those with dietary restrictions. For instance, if using protein powder to make a protein shake, selecting one labeled "plant-based" ensures it fits both the lactose-free and vegan requirements.

